This document describes the on-disk format, the concurrency model, the
command line and the internal package layout of {C:eictar}, and gives the
reason for each choice. {C:doc/format.md} is the specification of the bytes of
an archive. When the two do not agree, {C:doc/format.md} is correct. When the
code changes, change this document too. {C:testing.md} describes the tests
and the evidence that they give, and {C:history.md} gives the milestones and
the releases. Until 2026-10-15, they were {ref t=#testing:§13} and {ref t=#implementation-milestones:§16} of this document.

{C:problem_statement.md} and this document stay in agreement. The statement says
{i:what} the program does and {i:why}. This document says {i:how}. A change to a
requirement starts in the statement. Then it comes into {ref t=#decisions:§1.1} of this document.

