    {C:--verify} and {C:--diff} pass, and {C:--diff-extract} reports the content,
    at the byte that changed.
  }
  {item:
    {C:TestDiffExtractFindsFaultsOfExtraction} and
    {C:TestDiffExtractFindsAMissingAttribute}: a scratch directory that writes
    one wrong byte, a wrong mode or a wrong time, and a {C:setXattr} that sets
    nothing. Each gives one line {C:after extraction}.
  }
  {item:
    {C:TestDiffExtractComparesTimesToThePrecisionOfTheScratch}: a scratch
    directory that keeps times to 2 s gives no difference of time.
  }
  {item:
    {C:TestDiffExtractOfAnAttributeThatTheScratchRefuses}: no difference, and
    one notice.
  }
  {item:
    {C:TestDiffExtractFaultsAreNeverSilent} and
    {C:TestDiffExtractSourceFaultsAreNeverSilent}: each operation on the
    scratch directory, and each on the tree, fails in turn. Each fault fails
    the run with that fault, no handle stays open, and the scratch directory
    goes.
  }
  {item:
    {C:TestDiffExtractAsRoot}, in the CI job as root: a wrong owner of a copy,
    and other numbers of a device node, are each a difference.
  }
  {item:
    {C:TestDiffExtractReportsEachCauseOnce}, {C:TestDiffExtractOfAFullScratch},
    {C:TestDiffExtractOfADamagedArchive}, {C:TestDiffExtractRefusesAScratchInTheTree},
    {C:TestDiffExtractDoesNotDependOnWorkers}, and the tests of links, hardlinks,
